  "spatial_partition_note": "The main comparison builds the spatial partition ONCE (KMeans seeded with --seed0) and reuses it for every model, seed and scheme, so random-vs-spatial is a paired comparison. The SD across seeds of a spatial-CV cell therefore measures learner randomness only and is exactly 0.000 for deterministic models (ridge, PLS). The two uncertainties the fixed partition hides are reported separately: where the block boundaries fall (results.partition_sensitivity, methods kmeans_seed and grid_offset) and how many blocks are used (results.block_sensitivity). 2 KMeans seeds produced 1 distinct partition(s) (compared up to cluster renumbering), so the reported k-means blocking is insensitive to its own seed and its SD of 0.000 is a measured null rather than a varied estimate. Redrawing boundaries with a random rotation and grid origin gave 2 distinct partition(s); that spread is reported as results.boundary_sensitivity, together with the effect of the block count in results.block_sensitivity.",
